{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-ledger", "file": "references/single-demo-overreach.md", "content": "# Avoiding overreach from a single demo

A one-pair example can show a striking local color change, but does not by itself prove a broad rule such as filling an enclosure, propagating color across an object, or encoding every matching marker. Record the exact changed cells and equally important unchanged candidates before generalizing. Keep separate hypotheses for task class, selector, operation, and output representation; avoid collapsing all four into one intuitive visual story.

After a candidate fails, the failure rejects the entire candidate transformation. Reopen those four components rather than making a cosmetic adjustment. A retry should explain all observed edits and non-edits and, when more than one rule remains plausible, use a demo request only for a concrete distinguishing prediction.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484434/attempts/a51726d22484491ca3bb302d2d403d60/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-ledger/references/single-demo-overreach.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-task-delta-inference", "file": "references/demo-output-mapping.md", "content": "# Validate the demo's output mapping before transfer

A visually structured demo output is not evidence by itself for reflection, tiling, or stamping. After the first plausible but incorrect submission, reopen the task class and output representation before changing coordinates. Record input/output dimensions, map input rows, columns, objects, or symbols to output cells/regions, and compare that candidate mapping against every available pair. Treat exact full-demo reproduction as a prerequisite for submitting; a coherent pattern that fails even one demo is still an unvalidated guess. If requesting another demo, identify which competing mappings its predicted output would distinguish.
